  "goodToKnow": "Die Brauerei is a brewery. Germany has around 1,500, more than half of them in Bavaria, many tiny and family-run. The Bavarian Reinheitsgebot (purity law) of 1516 famously allowed beer to contain only water, barley and hops; yeast was added later once it was understood. Weihenstephan, near Munich, claims to be the world's oldest brewery still operating, dating to 1040. Brauen means to brew, and der Brauer is the brewer."
